(PROJECT OVERVIEW) Tj
0 -16 Td
( ) Tj
0 -16 Td
(Phish Detector is a phishing URL analysis toolkit with three first-class entry points: a) Tj
0 -16 Td
(FastAPI backend with Celery workers, a Typer based CLI for power users, and a Manifest v3) Tj
0 -16 Td
(browser extension that surfaces risk verdicts directly inside the browser. All components) Tj
0 -16 Td
(share a PostgreSQL datastore so analysis history is consistent regardless of the client.) Tj
0 -16 Td
( ) Tj
0 -16 Td
(The repository provides a docker-compose stack for local development and bundles) Tj
0 -16 Td
(infrastructure defaults \(Redis, Selenium, PostgreSQL\) alongside the Python services and web) Tj
0 -16 Td
(assets. This document captures the recommended workflow for contributors and end users.) Tj
0 -16 Td
( ) Tj
0 -16 Td
(SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE) Tj
0 -16 Td
( ) Tj
0 -16 Td
(The system starts with `backend/`, a FastAPI application that exposes `/api/analyze`,) Tj
0 -16 Td
(`/api/result/{task_id}`, and `/api/history`. Incoming requests enqueue Celery tasks which) Tj
0 -16 Td
(perform heuristic scoring, domain age lookups, and Selenium powered DOM inspection to flag) Tj
0 -16 Td
(risky form elements.) Tj
0 -16 Td
( ) Tj
0 -16 Td
(`cli/` hosts a Typer command line client that talks to the API, offering `analyze` and) Tj
0 -16 Td
(`history` commands with verdict aware output. `extension/` contains a Chromium compatible) Tj
0 -16 Td
(popup that submits URLs, polls task status, and renders the persisted history table.) Tj
0 -16 Td
( ) Tj
0 -16 Td
(PostgreSQL stores every analysis record and Redis serves as the Celery broker and result) Tj
0 -16 Td
(backend. Selenium Grid \(headless Chrome\) enables lightweight page rendering and credential) Tj
0 -16 Td
(field detection.) Tj
0 -16 Td
( ) Tj
0 -16 Td
(DEVELOPMENT WORKFLOW) Tj
0 -16 Td
( ) Tj
0 -16 Td
(Recommended steps when contributing to the repo:) Tj
0 -16 Td
( ) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- Install Docker and Docker Compose, then run `docker-compose up --build` at least once to) Tj
0 -16 Td
(    seed the database schema.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- Export environment overrides as needed \(`DATABASE_URL`, `REDIS_URL`, `SELENIUM_URL`,) Tj
0 -16 Td
(    `CORS_ALLOW_ORIGINS`\).) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- For backend changes, create a virtual environment and install `backend/requirements.txt`,) Tj
0 -16 Td
(    then run `uvicorn app.main:app --reload`.) Tj
0 -16 Td
(- Run Celery locally with `celery -A app.tasks worker --loglevel=info` while developing) Tj
0 -16 Td
(    tasks.) Tj
